      "hints": [
        "For midpoint $Q$, the position vector is the average of those of $P$ and $R$.",
        "Solve $\\mathbf{q}=\\frac12(\\mathbf{p}+\\mathbf{r})$ for $\\mathbf{r}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Because $Q$ is the midpoint of $PR$, $2\\mathbf{q}=\\mathbf{p}+\\mathbf{r}$.",
        "Therefore the position vector of $R$ is $\\mathbf{r}=2\\mathbf{q}-\\mathbf{p}$."
      ],
