      },
      "hints": [
        "Use the magnitude to obtain an equation in $a^2+b^2$.",
        "Perpendicularity gives a second equation; eliminate one variable and keep both roots."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$6^2+a^2+b^2=21^2$ gives $a^2+b^2=405$. The dot product condition is $6(3)+2a+2b=0$, so $b=-a-9$.",
        "$a^2+(-a-9)^2=405$ simplifies to $a^2+9a-162=0=(a-9)(a+18)$.",
        "Thus $(a,b)=(9,-18)$ or $(-18,9)$; both satisfy the magnitude and dot-product conditions."
      ],
